# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian {#hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Hamiltonian {#hamiltonian}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The key to this problem is a mathematical operator—the Hamiltonian, which represents the total energy of a system. For computational purposes, we can think of this Hamiltonian as a large matrix. The solutions we are looking for—specifically the system's ground state—are the lowest eigenvalues of this matrix. The challenge, however, is that for practical problems, this Hamiltonian matrix is very large. It grows exponentially with the size of the system, quickly becoming too big ($2^n$ where $n$ is the number of qubits) for even the most powerful supercomputers to store or solve directly.\n"
msgstr "Kunci kepada masalah ini ialah pengendali matematik — Hamiltonian, yang mewakili jumlah tenaga sistem. Untuk tujuan pengiraan, kita boleh menganggap Hamiltonian ini sebagai matriks besar. Penyelesaian yang kita cari — khususnya keadaan asas sistem — ialah nilai eigen terendah bagi matriks ini. Cabaran, walau bagaimanapun, ialah untuk masalah praktikal, matriks Hamiltonian ini sangat besar. Ia berkembang secara eksponen dengan saiz sistem, dengan cepat menjadi terlalu besar ($2^n$ di mana $n$ ialah bilangan qubit) untuk disimpan atau diselesaikan secara langsung walaupun oleh superkomputer yang paling berkuasa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"H_{0,0} & H_{0,1} & \\cdots & H_{0,N-1} \\\\\n"
"H_{1,0} & H_{1,1} & \\cdots & H_{1,N-1} \\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\\n"
"H_{N-1,0} & H_{N-1,1} & \\cdots & H_{N-1,N-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} \\quad (N=2^n)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"H_{0,0} & H_{0,1} & \\cdots & H_{0,N-1} \\\\\n"
"H_{1,0} & H_{1,1} & \\cdots & H_{1,N-1} \\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\\n"
"H_{N-1,0} & H_{N-1,1} & \\cdots & H_{N-1,N-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} \\quad (N=2^n)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To get around this, we use a powerful strategy known as the subspace method. Instead of tackling the whole matrix, we intelligently select a small, relevant slice — a \"subspace\" — that we believe contains the most important information about the low-energy solution we're looking for.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengatasi ini, kita menggunakan strategi yang berkuasa yang dikenali sebagai kaedah subruang. Daripada menangani keseluruhan matriks, kita memilih dengan bijak hirisan kecil yang relevan — \"subruang\" — yang kita percaya mengandungi maklumat terpenting tentang penyelesaian tenaga rendah yang kita cari.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\underset{\\text{Full Hamiltonian}}{\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\ddots & \\vdots \\\\\n"
"\\cdots & H_{i,j} & \\cdots \\\\\n"
"& \\vdots & \\ddots\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}}\n"
"\\quad \\xrightarrow{\\text{Project}} \\quad\n"
"\\underset{\\text{Projected Hamiltonian}}{\\tilde{H}}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle b_1 | H | b_1 \\rangle & \\cdots & \\langle b_1 | H | b_L \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\\n"
"\\langle b_L | H | b_1 \\rangle & \\cdots & \\langle b_L | H | b_L \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad \\xrightarrow{\\text{Diagonalize}} \\quad\n"
"\\underset{\\text{Eigenvalues}}{\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"E_0 & & 0 \\\\\n"
"& \\ddots & \\\\\n"
"0 & & E_{L-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\underset{\\text{Full Hamiltonian}}{\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\ddots & \\vdots \\\\\n"
"\\cdots & H_{i,j} & \\cdots \\\\\n"
"& \\vdots & \\ddots\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}}\n"
"\\quad \\xrightarrow{\\text{Project}} \\quad\n"
"\\underset{\\text{Projected Hamiltonian}}{\\tilde{H}}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle b_1 | H | b_1 \\rangle & \\cdots & \\langle b_1 | H | b_L \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\\n"
"\\langle b_L | H | b_1 \\rangle & \\cdots & \\langle b_L | H | b_L \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad \\xrightarrow{\\text{Diagonalize}} \\quad\n"
"\\underset{\\text{Eigenvalues}}{\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"E_0 & & 0 \\\\\n"
"& \\ddots & \\\\\n"
"0 & & E_{L-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once this small subspace is defined by a set of basis states $\\{|b_i\\rangle\\}$, the full Hamiltonian is projected onto it to create the new, smaller matrix $\\tilde{H}$. Each element of this matrix is calculated from the subspace basis states and the original Hamiltonian as in $\\langle b_i | H | b_j \\rangle$. This small matrix can then be easily diagonalized on a classical computer, and the resulting eigenvalues are our estimated energies.\n"
msgstr "Setelah subruang kecil ini ditakrifkan oleh set keadaan asas $\\{|b_i\\rangle\\}$, Hamiltonian penuh diunjurkan ke atasnya untuk mencipta matriks yang lebih kecil, $\\tilde{H}$. Setiap elemen matriks ini dikira daripada keadaan asas subruang dan Hamiltonian asal seperti dalam $\\langle b_i | H | b_j \\rangle$. Matriks kecil ini kemudian boleh dipeserakan dengan mudah pada komputer klasik, dan nilai eigen yang terhasil ialah anggaran tenaga kita.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As you might guess, the success of this entire approach heavily relies on choosing a \"good\" subspace. If our subspace does not accurately represent the true ground state, our final answer will be incorrect. This is where quantum computers come in: they allow us to prepare and sample from complex quantum states designed to identify these important subspaces. For truly massive problems, like complex chemical structures or binding sites, even the projected matrix may still be challenging to diagonalize. Thus, such problems are ideally-suited to leverage the strengths of both quantum and classical computing resources.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang mungkin anda jangkakan, kejayaan keseluruhan pendekatan ini sangat bergantung pada pemilihan subruang yang \"baik\". Jika subruang kita tidak mewakili dengan tepat keadaan asas sebenar, jawapan akhir kita akan salah. Di sinilah komputer kuantum berperanan: ia membolehkan kita menyediakan dan mengambil sampel daripada keadaan kuantum kompleks yang direka untuk mengenal pasti subruang penting ini. Untuk masalah yang benar-benar besar, seperti struktur kimia kompleks atau tapak pengikatan, walaupun matriks yang diunjurkan mungkin masih mencabar untuk dipeserakan. Oleh itu, masalah sedemikian sangat sesuai untuk memanfaatkan kekuatan kedua-dua sumber pengiraan kuantum dan klasik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following sections, we will explore two advanced algorithms, SQD and SKQD, which leverage quantum mechanics to find and construct these subspaces. For a deeper dive, there is a [full-length course](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms) on IBM Quantum learning devoted to these topics in detail. For our purposes in this course, we will keep the explanation at a high level.\n"
msgstr "Dalam bahagian berikutnya, kita akan meneroka dua algoritma lanjutan, SQD dan SKQD, yang memanfaatkan mekanik kuantum untuk mencari dan membina subruang ini. Untuk penerokaan yang lebih mendalam, terdapat [kursus penuh](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms) di IBM Quantum learning yang didedikasikan kepada topik-topik ini secara terperinci. Untuk tujuan kita dalam kursus ini, kita akan memastikan penjelasan pada peringkat tinggi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample-based Quantum Diagonalization {#sample-based-quantum-diagonalization}"
msgstr "Pepenjurusan Kuantum Berasaskan Sampel {#sample-based-quantum-diagonalization}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample-based Quantum Diagonalization (SQD) is a powerful variational algorithm that implements the subspace method in a quantum way. It avoids costly, complex procedures like Hadamard tests by using a quantum computer to prepare a trial state and sample *bitstrings*, which define the subspace for classical diagonalization.\n"
msgstr "Pepenjurusan Kuantum Berasaskan Sampel (SQD) ialah algoritma variasi yang berkuasa yang melaksanakan kaedah subruang dengan cara kuantum. Ia mengelakkan prosedur yang mahal dan kompleks seperti ujian Hadamard dengan menggunakan komputer kuantum untuk menyediakan keadaan percubaan dan mengambil sampel *rentetan bit*, yang menentukan subruang untuk pepenjurusan klasik.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A schematic of the workflow specific to sample-based quantum diagonalization. The steps include a variational quantum circuit, using measurements to project the Hamiltonian into a subspace, then using a classical optimizer to update variational parameters in the circuit and repeating.](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/sqd-skqd/sqd-cycle.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A schematic of the workflow specific to sample-based quantum diagonalization. The steps include a variational quantum circuit, using measurements to project the Hamiltonian into a subspace, then using a classical optimizer to update variational parameters in the circuit and repeating.](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/sqd-skqd/sqd-cycle.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The SQD algorithm can be broken down into the following steps:\n"
msgstr "Algoritma SQD boleh dipecahkan kepada langkah-langkah berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Prepare the Ansatz state {#step-1-prepare-the-ansatz-state}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Sediakan keadaan Ansatz {#step-1-prepare-the-ansatz-state}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let $H = \\sum_{j=1}^Q \\alpha_j P_j$ be the Hamiltonian on $n$ qubits. While the true ground state may be supported on all $2^n$ basis states, SQD is most effective in instances where the ground state can be well-approximated by a sparse subspace (a polynomially-sized set of bitstrings).\n"
msgstr "Biarkan $H = \\sum_{j=1}^Q \\alpha_j P_j$ ialah Hamiltonian pada $n$ qubit. Walaupun keadaan asas sebenar mungkin disokong pada semua $2^n$ keadaan asas, SQD paling berkesan dalam kes di mana keadaan asas boleh dihampirkan dengan baik oleh subruang yang jarang (set rentetan bit bersaiz polinomial).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To construct this subspace, we start with an input state $|\\phi_0\\rangle$, such as the Hartree-Fock (HF) state in chemistry. We then apply a parameterized quantum circuit, $U(\\theta)$, which is known as the ansatz.\n"
msgstr "Untuk membina subruang ini, kita bermula dengan keadaan input $|\\phi_0\\rangle$, seperti keadaan Hartree-Fock (HF) dalam kimia. Kita kemudian menggunakan Circuit kuantum berparameter, $U(\\theta)$, yang dikenali sebagai ansatz.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram showing the overlap of the computational basis states making up the ansatz and those making up the true ground state. Specifically, the image shows that the two regions will have some overlap, but might not perfectly match.](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/sqd-skqd/ansatz.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A diagram showing the overlap of the computational basis states making up the ansatz and those making up the true ground state. Specifically, the image shows that the two regions will have some overlap, but might not perfectly match.](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/sqd-skqd/ansatz.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This diagram illustrates the goal of a good ansatz. The ansatz prepares a quantum state whose support (the set of basis states it is composed of) should ideally have a large overlap with the support of the true ground state. This circuit allows us to quickly project the ansatz onto computational basis states, which will be further used in classical diagonalization. In other words: we don't have to guess an ansatz that is the ground state; we only need it to contain the same basis states. Then classical diagonalization of the projected Hamiltonian will give us the superposition of basis states that best approximates the ground state.\n"
msgstr "Rajah ini menggambarkan matlamat ansatz yang baik. Ansatz menyediakan keadaan kuantum yang sokongannya (set keadaan asas yang terdiri daripadanya) seharusnya mempunyai pertindanan besar dengan sokongan keadaan asas sebenar. Circuit ini membolehkan kita mengunjurkan ansatz dengan cepat kepada keadaan asas pengiraan, yang akan digunakan lebih lanjut dalam pepenjurusan klasik. Dalam erti kata lain: kita tidak perlu meneka ansatz yang merupakan keadaan asas; kita hanya perlu ia mengandungi keadaan asas yang sama. Kemudian pepenjurusan klasik Hamiltonian yang diunjurkan akan memberikan kita superposisi keadaan asas yang paling menghampiri keadaan asas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Sample the subspace {#step-2-sample-the-subspace}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Ambil sampel subruang {#step-2-sample-the-subspace}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By sampling from the circuit prepared by the ansatz, we get a collection of bitstrings, $\\{b_j\\}_{j=1}^L$. These bitstrings define the basis of our chosen subspace. The quantum runtime for this step is determined by the depth of the circuit and the number of samples taken.\n"
msgstr "Dengan mengambil sampel daripada Circuit yang disediakan oleh ansatz, kita mendapat koleksi rentetan bit, $\\{b_j\\}_{j=1}^L$. Rentetan bit ini menentukan asas subruang yang kita pilih. Masa jalan kuantum untuk langkah ini ditentukan oleh kedalaman Circuit dan bilangan sampel yang diambil.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Project and diagonalize classically {#step-3-project-and-diagonalize-classically}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Unjur dan peserakan secara klasik {#step-3-project-and-diagonalize-classically}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using the sampled bitstrings, we project the Hamiltonian into the subspace they span. For each pair of bitstrings $(j, k)$, we classically compute the matrix element $\\tilde{H}_{jk} = \\langle b_j | H | b_k \\rangle$. Because Pauli operators are sparse, this step is classically efficient for physical Hamiltonians. The resulting small matrix $\\tilde{H}$ is then diagonalized on a classical processor to estimate the ground state and its energy.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan rentetan bit yang diambil sampel, kita mengunjurkan Hamiltonian ke dalam subruang yang dicakupinya. Untuk setiap pasangan rentetan bit $(j, k)$, kita mengira secara klasik elemen matriks $\\tilde{H}_{jk} = \\langle b_j | H | b_k \\rangle$. Kerana pengendali Pauli adalah jarang, langkah ini cekap secara klasik untuk Hamiltonian fizikal. Matriks kecil yang terhasil $\\tilde{H}$ kemudian dipeserakan pada pemproses klasik untuk menganggarkan keadaan asas dan tenaganya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Optimize the ansatz (optional) {#step-4-optimize-the-ansatz-optional}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Optimumkan ansatz (pilihan) {#step-4-optimize-the-ansatz-optional}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The process can be made iterative. By treating the estimated ground state energy as a cost function, we can optimize the circuit parameters ($\\theta$) by using methods like gradient descent to improve the ansatz, and in turn, the energy approximation in the next iteration.\n"
msgstr "Proses ini boleh dijadikan berulang. Dengan memperlakukan anggaran tenaga keadaan asas sebagai fungsi kos, kita boleh mengoptimumkan parameter Circuit ($\\theta$) dengan menggunakan kaedah seperti kecerunan menurun untuk menambah baik ansatz, dan seterusnya, anggaran tenaga dalam lelaran seterusnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key advantages of SQD {#key-advantages-of-sqd}"
msgstr "Kelebihan utama SQD {#key-advantages-of-sqd}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQD offers several powerful features that make it a leading candidate for demonstrating quantum advantage:\n"
msgstr "SQD menawarkan beberapa ciri yang berkuasa yang menjadikannya calon utama untuk menunjukkan kelebihan kuantum:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Strong robustness to noise: Suppose the true ground state is supported on only two bitstrings. If these are sampled at all, even if their overlap with our ansatz is small, the diagonalization will assign them the appropriate weights and effectively ignore all other extraneous, noisy bitstrings that might have also been sampled. This inherent filtering makes SQD particularly noise-tolerant.\n"
msgstr "Ketahanan yang kuat terhadap hingar: Andaikan keadaan asas sebenar disokong hanya pada dua rentetan bit. Jika ini diambil sampel sama sekali, walaupun pertindanan mereka dengan ansatz kita kecil, pepenjurusan akan memberikan mereka pemberat yang sesuai dan secara berkesan mengabaikan semua rentetan bit asing dan bergelut lain yang mungkin juga telah diambil sampel. Penapisan semula jadi ini menjadikan SQD sangat tahan terhadap hingar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical verifiability: Unlike QPE or VQAs, SQD yields a classical approximation to the ground state. This means anyone with access to the list of bitstrings and their weights can recompute and verify the energy estimate directly on a classical computer.\n"
msgstr "Boleh disahkan secara klasik: Berbeza dengan QPE atau VQA, SQD menghasilkan anggaran klasik kepada keadaan asas. Ini bermakna sesiapa yang mempunyai akses kepada senarai rentetan bit dan pemberat mereka boleh mengira semula dan mengesahkan anggaran tenaga secara langsung pada komputer klasik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQD has already been used to estimate the ground-state dissociation energy of N$_2$ and the electronic properties of [2Fe-2S] and [4Fe-4S] clusters [[2]](#references), with circuits as large as 77 qubits and 10,570 gates.\n"
msgstr "SQD telah digunakan untuk menganggarkan tenaga pecahan keadaan asas N$_2$ dan sifat elektronik kluster [2Fe-2S] dan [4Fe-4S] [[2]](#references), dengan Circuit sebesar 77 qubit dan 10,570 gate.\n"

